intrusion in printed note 18; the English omits it.", "reason": "editorial_bracketing"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Hollow places follows Charles’s correction in printed note 19: the marked Ethiopic judgments corresponds to Greek κρίματα, which he regards as corrupt for κοιλώματα.", "reason": "editorial_emendation"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:9", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "*ወአውሥአኒ፡ ወይቤለኒ፡ እሉ፡ ፫ተገብሩ፡ ከመ፡ ይትፈለጥ፡ መንፈሶሙ፡ ለ*ምዉታን፡ ወከመዝ፡ ተፈልጠ፡ ለመንፈሶሙ፡ ለጻድቃን፡ ዘውእቱ፡ ነቅዐ፡ ማይ፡ በላዕሌሁ፡ ብርህት።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied selected Charles1906 edition candidate after two independent read-only review passes; recheck all current glyphs and editor supplies against five consecutive primary scans. No manuscript, human specialist or publication certification. Source or syntax at this unit remained HELD in the prior pass; do not approve by association with adjacent accepted units."}, "translation": {"text": "And he answered me, saying, “These three[a] were made to keep apart the spirits of the dead; and thus a place was set apart for the spirits of the righteous[b]. Above it was a spring of water, bright[c].”", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The printed text reads three whereas verse 2 reads four; the two counts are not harmonized.", "reason": "textual_variant"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The prefixed for the spirits of the righteous follows the Greek G-assisted edition supply in Charles note 28. The clause describes a place set apart for them, not the righteous spirits performing the separating.", "reason": "editorial_supply"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Charles note 32 emends the Ethiopic light noun ብርሃን to adjective ብርህት with Greek φωτεινή, following Flemming. Bright is provisionally attached to the spring; the antecedent of above it remains uncertain. This is not an independently attested Ethiopic manuscript reading.", "reason": "textual_uncertainty"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:10", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "በከመ፡ ከማሁ፡ ተፈጥረ፡ ለኃጥኣን፡ ሶበ፡ ይመውቱ፡ ወይትቀበሩ፡ ውስተ፡ ምድር፡ ወኵነኔ፡ ኢኮነ፡ በላዕሌሆሙ፡ በሕይወቶሙ።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied selected Charles1906 edition candidate after two independent read-only review passes; recheck all current glyphs and editor supplies against five consecutive primary scans. No manuscript, human specialist or publication certification."}, "translation": {"text": "Likewise, a place was made for sinners[a], when they die and are buried in the earth and judgment has not come upon them during their lifetime.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "A place is supplied from the surrounding description. The comparison introduces sinners discussed further in verse 11; the printed negative concerning judgment remains present.", "reason": "translation_explication"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:11", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "በዝየ፡ ይትፈለጥ፡ ነፍሶሙ፡ ዲበ፡ ዛቲ፡ ዐቢይ፡ ጻዕር፡ እስከ፡ አመ፡ ዐቢይ፡ ዕለት፡ እንተ፡ ኵነኔ፡ ወመቅሠፍት፡ ወጻዕር፡ ለእለ፡ ይረግሙ፡ እስከ፡ ለዓለም፡ ወበቀል፡ ለነፍሶሙ፡ በህየ፡ ይእስሮሙ፡ እስከ፡ ለዓለም፡ [ወእመኒ፡ ውእቱ፡ እምቅድመ፡ ዓለም።]", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied selected Charles1906 edition candidate after two independent read-only review passes; recheck all current glyphs and editor supplies against five consecutive primary scans. No manuscript, human specialist or publication certification."}, "translation": {"text": "Here their souls are set apart in this great affliction until the great day of judgment, punishment, and affliction for those who curse forever, and vengeance upon their souls.[a] There he will bind them forever.[b]", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Those who curse follows printed active ይረግሙ. Charles note 41 proposes passive ይትረገሙ, explained through Greek note 9, but it is not installed here. The attachment of forever within the punishment sequence is difficult.", "reason": "editorial_emendation"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Their souls continue the human sinners of verse 10. The agent of the binding is unnamed. The final bracketed Ethiopic clause is omitted following Charles note 44, which identifies it as an intrusion.", "reason": "editorial_bracketing"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:12", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወከመዝ፡ ተፈልጠ፡ ለነፍስ፡ እለ፡ ይስክዩ፡ እለ፡ ያርእዩ፡ በእንተ፡ ሕጉለት፡ አመ፡ *ተቀትሉ፡ በመዋዕለ፡ ኃጥኣን።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied selected Charles1906 edition candidate after two independent read-only review passes; recheck all current glyphs and editor supplies against five consecutive primary scans. No manuscript, human specialist or publication certification. Source or syntax at this unit remained HELD in the prior pass; do not approve by association with adjacent accepted units."}, "translation": {"text": "And likewise a division has been made for the souls of those who make accusation[a], who make known their destruction[b] when they were killed in the days of sinners.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or make their complaint; compare the accusation of verses 5–7.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The source names destruction; their supplies a contextual referent. A star is printed before the killing verb, but the reviewed apparatus does not establish its exact editorial provenance, so it is preserved without a manuscript or Greek-based claim.", "reason": "textual_uncertainty"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:13", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወከመዝ፡ ተፈጥረ፡ ለነፍሶሙ፡ ለሰብእ፡ እለ፡ ኢኮኑ፡ ጻድቃነ፡ አላ፡ ኃጥኣነ፡ እለ፡ ፍጹማነ፡ አበሳ፡ ወምስለ፡ አባሲ